; NPC answer to being given something
;
; Script handler (op 3 in #R$C82D) of behaviour $1D, the behaviour switched on
; by the event "give" (command id $1D) for Gandalf, Thorin, the wood elf, the
; butler and Elrond. The character speaks: usually "Thank you", sometimes (a
; random number from 0 to 10 of 8 or more) "What do you expect me to do with
; this ?". Always passes the test pass of the script engine (#R$9D44).
; .
; Hardware: none (the text goes through the message printer).
@label=NpcAnswersGift
c$A4DF CALL $9D44    ; test pass: allowed, nothing else
 $A4E2 LD A,$0A
 $A4E4 CALL $9C9F    ; random 0 to 10
 $A4E7 LD HL,$B0A6   ; "What do you expect me to do with this ?"
 $A4EA CP $08        ; 8 or more
 $A4EC JP NC,$A1E3
 $A4EF LD HL,$B047   ; "Thank you"
 $A4F2 JP $A1E3
